;W[md];B[ne];W[qc];B[qd]C[This is necessary. To plat at 33 instead would be contrary to the spirit of 15 and 25.]
;W[pc];B[oc];W[ob];B[od];W[mb];B[me];W[ld];B[le];W[nj]LB[mm:A]C[This invasion is too deep. Had white exchanged 62 for 63, and then played at 'A' the game would have been quite even.]
;B[dq];W[cq];B[dl]C[This is an excellant move, played on a very large scale. As well as its effect on the corner, it has implications towards the white stone at 40. ]
;W[dp];B[lm]C[White is at a loss as to how to extricate his stone, because his escape is blocked by 43.]
;W[pk];B[qk];W[qj];B[ok];W[pl];B[ql];W[pi];B[oj];W[oi];B[qi];W[rj];B[ri];W[qh];B[rh]
;W[mh];B[ol];W[ke];B[kf];W[kh]C[The sequence up to here sees white trying to reduce some of black's territory while making eye-shape for himself. However, 64 at 67 would give better shape for white.]
;B[li];W[mi];B[lj];W[lh];B[ih]C[Black is back on the attack again. If white escapes towards the centre, black will make territory on the left; if towards the upper side, black will destroy a large part of it.]
