;W[jd]C[Ill advised. Had white played 90, black could have captured two stones, but then white would have sente.]
;B[jc];W[kc];B[ie];W[kd];B[ij]C[A curious move. If played at 90, white would be left in real trouble.]
;W[ii];B[hi];W[jh];B[jj];W[gi];B[hj];W[gg]LB[ff:B]C[This move threatens the move at 'B'. With the sequence to 109, black secures central territory. However, his position still has a few defects.]
